WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.480
Threat actor profiling is a defensive intelligence activity.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:12.820
The purpose is to understand likely behaviors, objectives, capabilities, targeting patterns, and tradecraft so an organization can make better security decisions.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.240
A profile is not a trophy label or a public accusation.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:28.060
A useful profile helps defenders decide what to monitor, which detections to improve, which risks to prioritize, and how to communicate a threat in language the organization can act on.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.800
AI can assist with the heavy analytic workload around profiling.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:41.620
It can summarize long reports, cluster observations, draft profile sections, compare patterns across cases, build timelines, and identify analytic gaps.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.840
It can help analysts move from scattered notes to a structured view of behavior.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:54.220
The value is speed and consistency, especially when analysts are reviewing many reports, telemetry summaries, incident notes, and intelligence updates.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:01:00.920
Actor profiling is different from attribution, incident response, threat hunting, and vulnerability management.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:05.940
Attribution asks who may be behind activity and with what confidence.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.600
Incident response contains and investigates an event.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.460
Threat hunting searches for evidence in an environment.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.400
Vulnerability management reduces known weaknesses.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:25.540
Profiling can support all of those activities, but it is its own analytic product: a defensible description of behavior, intent, capability, and uncertainty.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.640
AI output must be grounded in evidence and reviewed by human analysts.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:36.860
A model can write a fluent profile even when the evidence is weak, circular, stale, or misunderstood.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:44.280
Human review protects the organization from overconfidence, unsupported claims, privacy mistakes, and sensational reporting.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.220
The goal is not to name actors for its own sake.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:52.640
The goal is better defensive planning, detection, prioritization, readiness, and communication.
